Rule 1 (two lists must have the same number of elements)
{v_1: list(int ⊎ float ⊎ list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)), v_2: list(int ⊎ float ⊎ list(int) ⊎ tuple(int))} |= v_1.len = v_2.len
