Rule 3 (disable strict sequence type checking to avoid TypeError differences)
{v_1: bool} |= v_1 = false
>>
Rule 4 (if composites are not expanded, also disable strict type checking)
{v_1: bool, v_2: bool} |= if v_2 then true else v_1 = false
>>
Rule 5 (both lists are either empty or both non-empty with equal size)
{v_1: list(int), v_2: list(int)} |= (v_1.len = 0 ∧ v_2.len = 0) ∨ (v_1.len > 0 ∧ v_2.len > 0 ∧ v_1.len = v_2.len)
